{
  "requirement": "When `habeas status` or `habeas status --all` displays a Markdown table, it MUST left-align and space-pad the Definition and Evidence columns so every row, including the header and separator row, has its `|` column delimiters in the same positions. Column widths MUST be determined by the widest displayed cell in each column.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** the requirement is met. `render_evidence_table` implements it, it is marked `{impl}`, and a test covers it.\n\n**Implementation** (`src/markdown.rs`, `render_evidence_table`, marked `{impl}` for `requirements.cli.status_table_alignment`):\n- It computes each column width as the maximum of the cell lengths and the header text. These are `\"Definition\".len()` and `\"Evidence\".len()`.\n- It formats the header row, the `---` separator row and every data row with the same `{:<width$}` left-align and space-pad format. All rows therefore have their `|` delimiters in the same positions.\n- `status_markdown_with_options` in `src/commands.rs` calls it for both `habeas status` and `habeas status --all`. The same function serves both modes, so the behaviour is not duplicated.\n- The width uses byte length (`.len()`) rather than character count. That is safe here because the cells are ASCII. Definition names pass `valid_name`, which allows only ASCII alphanumerics plus `_`, `-` and `.`. The kind nouns and the evidence state labels are static ASCII strings.\n- The function is also reused by the index page (`src/index.rs`), under `requirements.cli.shared_status_rendering`. That reuse is specified by that requirement and is marked on the function.\n- I found no other unmarked code that renders status tables, and no unspecified behaviour in the rendering code.\n\n**Test** (`tests/commands.rs`, `status_tables_align_each_column_to_its_widest_cell`, marked `{test}`):\n- It runs both `status` and `status --all` against a fixture and extracts the table lines.\n- It asserts the table has more than two lines (header, separator and at least one data row).\n- It asserts that every line, including the header and separator, has `|` at identical byte offsets.\n- It asserts each cell has a single leading space, which gives left alignment, and a trailing space.\n- It asserts that each column's inner width equals the widest trimmed cell in that column. This covers \"widest displayed cell\".\n- It asserts that the separator row cells are `---`.\n\nThis covers both commands, the header, separator and data rows, and the width rule. The one case it does not cover is non-ASCII cells, which the system cannot produce.",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.cli.status_table_alignment",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.cli.status_table_alignment"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} status_table_alignment",
        "When `habeas status` or `habeas status --all` displays a Markdown table, it MUST left-align and space-pad the Definition and Evidence columns so every row, including the header and separator row, has its `|` column delimiters in the same positions. Column widths MUST be determined by the widest displayed cell in each column.",
        ":::"
      ]
